      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This is a profound concern that touches on the very definition of \"good art\" in a post-modern context, as shifting the metric from objective craft to subjective political alignment risks narrow cultural polarization. While the momentum toward visibility is undeniable, it is perilous for contemporary art to abandon the classic \"critical engagement\" required to question the very political agendas it champions. If only one narrative dominates, we risk creating a divisive \"correct\" art that paralyzes the dialogue rather than expands it into something truly universal.",
      "source": "target",
